<title>SINGAPORE: Isetan six months net profit up.</title>
<headline>Isetan six months net profit up.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to September 30 1996.</p>
<p>	   (in millions of Singapore $ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			0.95	 vs    (1.74)</p>
<p>    Group shares (cts)	    0.03	 vs    (0.05)</p>
<p>    Turnover			122.07	 vs   115.41</p>
<p>    Investment income	     0.17	 vs     0.13</p>
<p>    Other income		    4.35	 vs     4.41</p>
<p>    Interest expense		0.001	vs     0.26</p>
<p>    Depreciation, amortisation  3.64	 vs     3.21</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries		 1.08	 vs     nil</p>
<p>Note - Isetan (Singapore) Ltd said the extraordinaries were from its disposal of a condominium unit and sale of a long term investment in a sister company.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
